#2114
Beside a Deep Well~
   An old stone well stands in a confusion of paths here, its
windlass rotted and its bucket long since gone.  A look down the
shaft finds only darkness and a smell of cold rot; someone has
thrown bones down it, and they lie white on the wet stones below.
Paths part to the north, south and west, and the manor waits
east.
